00:55.460 --> 01:02.600
If it's going to throw some more chop solidation sideways and even left translation and failure in the daily cycles, then it'd be time to flip short and head for some cycle lows.

01:02.720 --> 01:11.880
But something tells me based on my sentiment read at the moment, it's not a high conviction sentiment read, but I look around and the sentiment to me says, I think we've got a good chance of going to new highs for the market.

01:12.060 --> 01:14.400
So the first thing I wanted to point out today is this.

01:14.400 --> 01:23.480
OK, this was all over my timeline this morning that the US and Japan have got an alliance with Friday's coordinated foreign exchange actions countering disorderly yen movements.

01:23.720 --> 01:28.180
There's a lot of speculation about the yen carry trade and Japan having to defend its currency.

01:28.180 --> 01:34.160
The Treasury has said it remains a tentative and in close communication with our counterparts at the MOF and the BOJ.

01:34.160 --> 01:38.040
They say they will not hesitate to participate further in joint intervention.

01:38.400 --> 01:41.800
And they've got this new FEMA repo facility, which is an important backstop.

01:42.140 --> 01:53.660
And frankly, this is all quite a wordy way of saying that the Fed has now provided a facility to allow Japan to borrow dollars against the Treasuries and then sell those dollars to buy yen and thus defend its currency,

01:54.160 --> 01:57.560
which stops them just dumping the Treasuries and forcing the yields higher.

01:57.560 --> 02:00.380
So we've got this weird form of yield curve control now.

02:00.560 --> 02:08.420
And yes, it does sound like a circus, but really, it's pretty interesting to me that this has all occurred perfectly into a daily cycle low window for the Dixie.

02:08.540 --> 02:17.680
And with the yields around seven weeks away from putting in a major weekly cycle high and looking for a major weekly cycle decline at the same time as the long end,

02:17.800 --> 02:24.880
which I use TLT as my proxy, is staging its fake breakdown, its sweep of the lows at long last, which we've been talking about potentially seeing since February.

02:24.880 --> 02:31.520
And again, it is only around seven weeks away now from not only a weekly cycle low, but also its seven and a half year cycle low,

02:31.620 --> 02:34.940
which I then maintain something like this is coming next.

02:35.240 --> 02:44.780
So super interesting times, but as scary as this might sound and as much as people love to hop on X and engagement farm and tell you it's the yen carry trade 2.0 and all of this kind of stuff.

02:44.860 --> 02:48.860
OK, I'm just in the camp of people that says I don't think that is a useful stance to take.

02:48.940 --> 02:51.960
I think it's better to just trade the cycles and let the stops do the worrying.

02:51.960 --> 03:00.140
As ever, you do you. But under the hood at the start of the year, the S&P 500 was expected to see earnings growth of around 13 percent for 2026.

03:00.320 --> 03:06.580
And as of right now, it's up 28 percent, meaning under the hood, I think we can indeed run this thing hotter for longer.

03:06.760 --> 03:10.580
And all this while the average stock price reaction is in line with historical norms.

03:10.700 --> 03:18.100
The season has been extraordinary for the Mag 7 and the group is on track to post nearly 40 percent net income growth year over year.

03:18.100 --> 03:22.640
And as I've been talking about in the level three members section, if we're going to see this thing run hotter for longer,

03:22.640 --> 03:27.320
we should really expect the Mag 7 to start to bust out now and drag the indices higher.

03:27.480 --> 03:34.540
Now, here's the key part. On average, the Mag 7 stocks have recorded price reactions to earnings results that are nearly double their five year norm.

03:34.720 --> 03:41.440
So just as you think everything's already overvalued, just as you think that it's dangerous buying at all time highs and this thing can't possibly go any higher.

03:41.440 --> 03:47.360
It looks like we are on pace here to see the leaders resume their leading to the upside, dragging the indices higher.

03:47.600 --> 03:52.260
And as crazy as it sounds, it may well be conducive to the completion of this fractal.

03:52.360 --> 03:59.060
OK, this would be extremely right translated in the four year cycle, which would imply we're going to come down very hard and fast in a black swan style plunge.

03:59.180 --> 04:03.160
But in the meantime, OK, I don't think it's wise to worry about that or speculate on that.

04:03.240 --> 04:06.740
I think it's just a case of let's see if we can bust through to new highs this week.

04:06.960 --> 04:09.160
